<p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse&gt;</span> <span class="dito">second edition</span></p>

<p>In the first edition I said you had arrived in time to see the beginning. Well, the beginning turned into work. Now there are things being raised here. We chose the language the world would be written in, and then we switched. The first one we left behind, and now the world is written in C#. The first engines started to be born, one piece at a time. We even tried to stand the 3D up. None of this existed a month ago. I like this part, the part where everything is still possible and nothing has thrown an error yet.</p>

<p>A build is a living thing while it compiles. Afterward it decides what it will be, and not everything we raise stays standing... but that belongs to another date. For now it is all upright, all new, and nobody needs to know the rest yet. Turn the page. The scaffolding is the beautiful part.</p>
